      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(android): require explicit retry after interrupted sends",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Android could resend a chat command after the app was killed after the gateway accepted it but before the local outbox row was deleted.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nInterrupted `sending` rows now become visible failed rows with a delivery-unconfirmed reason. The existing user-driven Retry action remains the only path that can replay an ambiguous command.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAndroid no longer silently repeats agent runs or tool side effects after a crash/restart when gateway deduplication is unavailable. Users can inspect, delete, or explicitly retry the affected command.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `./gradlew :app:testThirdPartyDebugUnitTest --tests ai.openclaw.app.chat.RoomChatCommandOutboxTest --tests ai.openclaw.app.chat.ChatControllerOutboxTest :app:runKtlintCheckOverMainSourceSet :app:runKtlintCheckOverTestSourceSet` — passed.\n- Room regression proves interrupted rows become `Failed` with the delivery-unconfirmed marker while preserving retry bookkeeping.\n- Controller regression proves startup shows the failed row instead of automatically flushing it.\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --engine codex --thinking high` — clean.\n- Remote Testbox proof is blocked because this environment is not authenticated to the `openclaw` Blacksmith organization; CI is required for the pushed head.\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex.\n",
        "branch": "codex/fix-android-outbox-ambiguous-delivery",
